From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:15:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: do not let a BO shared through dma-buf become
 purgeable

On the Gemini desktop, QtWebEngine imported dma-bufs of BOs their owner had marked
purgeable, about once per video frame, and panfrost_gem_open warned each time,
1466 times in one session. The shrinker could purge such a BO under the process
that just imported it.

madvise already refuses DONTNEED for a BO with more than one user it can see.
Refuse it too while the BO is exported or imported, since its other users only
show up when they import it.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c
index 75113073c..ed2061706 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c
@@ -503,6 +503,15 @@ static int panfrost_ioctl_madvise(struct drm_device *dev, void *data,
 			ret = -EINVAL;
 			goto out_unlock_mappings;
 		}
+
+		/*
+		 * A BO shared through dma-buf has users this driver cannot see
+		 * until they import it, so it must never be purged under them.
+		 */
+		if (gem_obj->dma_buf || drm_gem_is_imported(gem_obj)) {
+			ret = -EINVAL;
+			goto out_unlock_mappings;
+		}
 	}
 
 	args->retained = drm_gem_shmem_madvise_locked(&bo->base, args->madv);
